      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bcc7ea921c4762f82293cc3|full_name}: Yeah, but there must by other ways to prevent that. And there are. Especially if we go to let's say 500k polygons, you can do pretty good looking avatars with that. One possibility would be to make the viewability of avatars dependend on client systems and/or settings. Users could decide to just replace high-poly avatars from other users if those would slow down their systems or dump their framerate. Another solution would be an automatic system to reduce avatars polygons client-dependend. And I'm pretty sure there are more.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
