        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm honestly surprised to see a post like this. 72k is a generous number, if you need more than that you're doing something wrong. There's severe diminishing returns on the smoothness of a surface as you go higher, and physically modeling details/roughness is a bad way to work, you need to rely more on proper texture mapping to create details. The Fortnite avatars going around look excellent, despite being only 20-30k, because of the textures. Just be thankful the 20k limit is gone.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
