      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c5dbb67e736e74a8adc8630",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Strange that 90% of the avatars I see when I go into Vrchat, the avatars are not of that type where you need a super-high polygon count. Most are cartoonish/anime style avatars. I don't \"like\" the cartoonish, stylized avatars and more like \"natural\" ones, and I had good results without going crazy with polygons. You can always decimate.\n\nAlso, IMO it wouldn't make sense to do away with the polygon limit, but leave other limits (particles, materials, shaders etc.) in place. What about them?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
