      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If your model is above 70k then it's best to decimate or retopologize it. The devs want a lot of people in a room and if everyone had 300k+ poly models it would cause issues. If you want more details use normal, roughness, height, ect textures instead of polygons. You can always bake a normal map of a high poly model onto a low poly version.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
